-------------------------------------------------------------
 Ghostty keybinds  ·  Doomslayer  ·  prefix = Ctrl+B

 HOW: press Ctrl+B, RELEASE it, then the action key.
      (Not a chord — same idea as tmux prefix.)

 Ctrl+B ?         command palette (search actions/binds)
 Ctrl+B Ctrl+H    this cheat sheet in less (shell prompt)
 Esc              cancel prefix mode
 CLI:             ghostty +list-keybinds
-------------------------------------------------------------

  PREFIX
    Ctrl+B            enter prefix mode (one shot)
    Esc               cancel prefix mode
    b  or  Ctrl+B     send real Ctrl+B to the app (after prefix)

  TABS  (~ tmux windows)
    Ctrl+B c          new tab
    Ctrl+B n / p      next / previous tab
    Ctrl+B l / 0      last tab
    Ctrl+B 1 … 9      go to tab N
    Ctrl+B ,          rename tab
    Ctrl+B w          tab overview
    Ctrl+B d          close whole tab (all splits in it)

  WINDOWS
    Ctrl+B Shift+c    new window
    Ctrl+B &          close window

  SPLITS  (~ tmux panes)
    Ctrl+B h          horizontal split  (left | right)
    Ctrl+B v          vertical split    (top / bottom)
    Ctrl+B %          same as h
    Ctrl+B "          same as v
    Ctrl+B ←↓↑→       focus split
    Ctrl+B R          resize MODE (then arrows/hjkl; Esc exits)
    Ctrl+B Ctrl+←…→   one-shot resize
    Ctrl+B Shift+hjkl focus split (vim)
    Ctrl+B o / ;      next / previous split
    Ctrl+B z          zoom / unzoom pane
    Ctrl+B =          equalize splits
    Ctrl+B Ctrl+←↓↑→  resize split

  SEARCH / SCROLL
    Ctrl+B f  or  /   start search
    Ctrl+B [ / ]      page up / page down
    Ctrl+B g / G      scroll top / bottom
    Ctrl+B a          select all

  MISC
    Ctrl+B ?          VIEW KEYBINDS — command palette
    Ctrl+B Ctrl+H     VIEW KEYBINDS — this cheat sheet (less)

    Ctrl+B r          reload config
    Ctrl+B Enter      toggle fullscreen
    Ctrl+B i          terminal inspector

  NOTES
    · Shell Ctrl+D already exits a pane (EOF) — no prefix needed.
    · Prefix+d closes the tab; prefix+& closes the OS window.
    · h/v use tmux naming: h = side-by-side, v = stacked.
